# Vulnerability details

## Impact
There always gonna be a loss of 1 wei if the totalProtocolFee is odd number which can add up to much bigger loss because this is being calculated on every trade. 
## Proof of Concept
Due to the way `accumulatedProtocolRevenue` and `accumulatedCreatorRevenue` are calculated, there will be a loss of 1 wei every time if the `totalProtocolFee` is an odd number. 

```solidity

    function applyInterestForPoolStatus(Perp.AssetPoolStatus storage poolStatus, uint256 lastUpdateTimestamp, uint8 fee)
        internal
        returns (uint256 interestRate, uint256 totalProtocolFee)
    {
        if (block.timestamp <= lastUpdateTimestamp) {
            return (0, 0);
        }
        uint256 utilizationRatio = poolStatus.tokenStatus.getUtilizationRatio(); // Get utilization ratio
        // Skip calculating interest if utilization ratio is 0
        if (utilizationRatio == 0) {
            return (0, 0);
        }

        // Calculates interest rate
        interestRate = InterestRateModel.calculateInterestRate(poolStatus.irmParams, utilizationRatio)
            * (block.timestamp - lastUpdateTimestamp) / 365 days;


        totalProtocolFee = poolStatus.tokenStatus.updateScaler(interestRate, fee);
    ->    poolStatus.accumulatedProtocolRevenue += totalProtocolFee / 2;
    ->   poolStatus.accumulatedCreatorRevenue += totalProtocolFee / 2;
    } 
```

Here, we see that `accumulatedProtocolRevenue` and `accumulatedCreatorRevenue` should each account for 50% of the totalProtocol fee. However, due to precision loss, the fees will not be distributed equally, leading to a fee loss.

For example, if the totalProtocolFee is 99, then based on this calculation, `accumulatedProtocolRevenue` will be 99/2 = 54 and `accumulatedCreatorRevenue` will also be 99/2 = 54. This discrepancy occurs due to rounding down in solidity, resulting in a total of 54+54 = 98, not 99.

## Tools Used
Manual review

## Recommended Mitigation Steps
Consider subtracting the 50% from totalProtocolFee when calculating accumulatedCreatorRevenue 

```solidity
totalProtocolFee = poolStatus.tokenStatus.updateScaler(interestRate, fee); //99
poolStatus.accumulatedProtocolRevenue += totalProtocolFee / 2;//54
poolStatus.accumulatedCreatorRevenue += totalProtocolFee - totalProtocolFee/2;//99-54=55
```




