# Vulnerability details

## Impact 

- The [PriceFeed::getSqrtPrice()](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-05-predy/blob/a9246db5f874a91fb71c296aac6a66902289306a/src/PriceFeed.sol#L45) function lacks a freshness check. This function determines the value of various LP tokens. Inaccuracies can result in price deviations for LP tokens, affecting asset price calculations.

## Description

During market volatility or "flash crashes," if Chainlink's feed isn't promptly updated, the smart contract might continue using outdated token valuations.

Chainlink recommends that developers validate the `updatedAt` timestamp before using prices:

>"Your application should track the `latestTimestamp` or use the `updatedAt` value from `latestRoundData()` to ensure the answer is recent enough. If the answer isn't updated within an acceptable time frame (determined by your application), pause or switch operations."

On Arbitrum, the [heartbeat interval]((https://docs.chain.link/docs/arbitrum-price-feeds/)) is typically 1 hour.

```solidity
