IUniswapV3MintCallback(msg.sender).uniswapV3MintCallback(amount0, amount1, data);

//

IUniswapV3MintCallback(msg.sender).uniswapV3MintCallback(
    amount0Owed,
    amount1Owed,
    data
);
```
`msg.sender` in this case is the contract that called the `mint` function, and it is expected to implement the `IUniswapV3MintCallback` interface correctly.

